course: dictionary
lesson: 12480
title: Deletion: taking things away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A deletion is the act of removing something. The word comes from the verb delete, which means to take something out. A writer makes deletions when they cross out words that are not needed. «I made several deletions in my essay» means I removed several words or sentences from my essay.
explain: Deletion is used with computers and phones too. Deleting a photo or a message is a deletion. Often a deleted file is still kept in the bin or in a backup, so it is not gone for good yet. Context helps here: the words around deletion tell you it is about taking something away.
explain: Deletion can also mean the thing that was removed. «The editor's deletions made the story much shorter» means the removed parts made the story shorter. Ask yourself: is the word describing the action of removing, or the things that were removed? The sentence will show you which.
fact: A deletion is the act of removing something.
fact: «Deletion» comes from the verb «delete», which means to take something out.
fact: In writing, deletions are words or sentences you cross out because you do not need them.
fact: «Permanent deletion» means something is removed for good, so it cannot be got back.
fact: In science, a deletion can mean the loss of a part of a gene or chromosome.
exercise: «I made several deletions in my essay.» What is a deletion? | A kind of bird | *Something removed, such as crossed-out words | A new sentence added to the end | A loud noise in class
exercise: Which of these is a deletion? | Reading a book quietly | Drawing a picture of a cat | Writing a new title at the top | *Crossing out two extra words in a story
exercise: The verb linked to deletion, meaning to take something out, is | sleep | *delete | run
test: Mia pressed the button and her photo was gone for ever. What is this process called? | *Deletion | Division | Addition | Decoration
test: Which phrase means something is removed for good? | Temporary pause | Shared folder | *Permanent deletion | Quick look
exam: Read this: «The editor's deletions made the story much shorter.» What does deletions mean here? | Pictures in the story | Things that were added | *Things that were removed | People who wrote the story
